.TH LIBTOOL-NEXT-VERSION "1" "July 2026" "GNU libtool 2.6.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
libtool-next-version \- Determines next version to use for a libtool library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B libtool-next-version
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,PREVIOUS-LIBRARY CURRENT-LIBRARY\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Determines the next version to use for a libtool library.
.PP
PREVIOUS\-LIBRARY is the installed library (in .a or .so format) of the
previous release.
.PP
CURRENT\-LIBRARY is the installed library (in .a or .so format) of the current
release candidate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
print this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
print version information and exit
.PP
Send patches and bug reports to <bug\-libtool@gnu.org>.
